  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "pNpYk8jj62FVi5AB+FtQY4AQw6I=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:33:20.543Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "Two of the flag's statements about Sopra Steria Netherlands are about the record rather than the firm: post-merger Dutch revenue is not yet separable, and integration is still in progress with an unstable org chart. Its recorded stack is Microsoft and Salesforce, across public, banking, insurance and healthcare.\n\nEach of those blocks a different decision. Revenue that cannot be separated from the group's makes the size input to the score unreliable, and size is one of only two inputs the mechanical rescore used. An unstable org chart removes the durable owner that outreach needs: whoever holds a platform decision during an integration may not hold it when the structure settles, so effort spent building a relationship can evaporate without any change in the firm's interest.\n\nThe practical reading is that this row is time-dependent rather than settled. Its verticals are strong and its Dutch profile matches the pilot's targets, but nothing can be fixed about it until the integration concludes. Its UK sibling is scored separately on the same recorded stack and carries none of these caveats, which is worth remembering before the two rows are treated as one account.\n\n---\n\n## Leads sharing this finding (1)\n\n**9 \u00b7 do not pitch**\n- Sopra Steria Netherlands (NL)\n\nVerbatim research text this claim was extracted from:\n\n> DERIVED, NOT SCORED ON v3 \u2014 v2 row rescored mechanically (size + slot-occupancy only). Run the OSS-portfolio screen before acting. v2 verticals: Public, banking, insurance, healthcare \u00b7 NL profile: insurance, banking, healthcare, public \u00b7 rev 450000000 \u00b7 Post-merger NL revenue not yet separable. Integration still in progress - org chart unstable.",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-19T11:33:20.543496Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:33:20.543501Z"
    }
  },
